 "lines": [
  [
   "P1",
   "Title: Characterization of Natural Transformation Between Bifunctors/Sufficient Condition"
  ],
  [
   "P2",
   "Let $\\mathbf C, \\mathbf D$ and $\\mathbf E$ be [[Definition:Category|categories]]."
  ],
  [
   "P3",
   "Let $F, G : \\mathbf C \\times \\mathbf D \\to \\mathbf E$ be [[Definition:Bifunctor|bifunctors]] from the [[Definition:Product Category|product category]] $\\mathbf C \\times \\mathbf D$ to the [[Definition:Category|category]] $\\mathbf E$."
  ],
  [
   "P4",
   "For each [[Definition:Object (Category Theory)|object]] $C \\in\\mathbf C$ let: "
  ],
  [
   "P5",
   ":$F \\tuple{C, -}$ and $G \\tuple{C, -}$"
  ],
  [
   "P6",
   "denote the [[Definition:Functor|functors]] obtained by [[Definition:Bifunctor|substituting the first variable]] of $F$ and $G$, respectively, with $C$."
  ],
  [
   "P7",
   "For each [[Definition:Object (Category Theory)|object]] $D \\in\\mathbf D$ let:"
  ],
  [
   "P8",
   ":$F \\tuple{-, D}$ and $G \\tuple{-, D}$"
  ],
  [
   "P9",
   "denote the [[Definition:Functor|functors]] obtained by [[Definition:Bifunctor|substituting the second variable]] of $F$ and $G$, respectively, with $D$."
  ],
  [
   "P10",
   "For each [[Definition:Object (Category Theory)|object]] $\\tuple{C, D} \\in \\mathbf C \\times \\mathbf D$ let:"
  ],
  [
   "P11",
   ":$\\alpha_{\\tuple{C, D}} : F \\tuple{C,D} \\to G \\tuple{C,D}$ "
  ],
  [
   "P12",
   "denote a [[Definition:Morphism (Category Theory)|morphism]] in $\\mathbf E$."
  ],
  [
   "P13",
   "Let:"
  ],
  [
   "P14",
   ":$(1)\\quad$ For each [[Definition:Object (Category Theory)|object]]  $C \\in \\mathbf C : \\alpha \\tuple{C, -} : F \\tuple{C, -} \\to G \\tuple{C, -}$ be a [[Definition:Natural Transformation|natural transformation]]"
  ],
  [
   "P15",
   ":$(2)\\quad$ For each [[Definition:Object (Category Theory)|object]]  $D \\in \\mathbf D : \\alpha \\tuple{-, D} : F \\tuple{-, D} \\to G \\tuple{-, D}$ be a [[Definition:Natural Transformation|natural transformation]]"
  ],
  [
   "P16",
   "where:"
  ],
  [
   "P17",
   ":for [[Definition:Object (Category Theory)|objects]] $C \\in \\mathbf C$ and $D \\in \\mathbf D$, $\\alpha \\tuple{C, -}_D = \\alpha_{\\tuple{C, D}}$"
  ],
  [
   "P18",
   "and:"
  ],
  [
   "P19",
   ":for [[Definition:Object (Category Theory)|objects]] $C \\in \\mathbf C$ and $D \\in \\mathbf D$, $\\alpha \\tuple{-, D}_C = \\alpha_{\\tuple{C, D}}$"
  ],
  [
   "P20",
   "Then:"
  ],
  [
   "P21",
   ":$\\alpha : F \\to G$ is a [[Definition:Natural Transformation|natural transformation]]"
  ],
  [
   1,
   "== Proof 1 =="
  ],
  [
   2,
   "By definition of [[Definition:Natural Transformation|natural transformation]]:"
  ],
  [
   3,
   ":for all [[Definition:Morphism (Category Theory)|morphisms]] $f: C \\to C' \\in \\mathbf C$ and $g: D \\to D' \\in \\mathbf D$ the following [[Definition:Commutative Diagram|diagrams commute]]:"
  ],
  [
   4,
   ""
  ],
  [
   5,
   "::<nowiki>$\\begin{xy}"
  ],
  [
   6,
   "<0em,0em>*+{\\map {F \\tuple{-, D} } C} = \"FCD\","
  ],
  [
   7,
   "<15em,0em>*+{\\map {F \\tuple{-, D} } {C'} } = \"FC2D\","
  ],
  [
   8,
   "<0em,-6em>*+{\\map {G \\tuple{-, D} } C} = \"GCD\","
  ],
  [
   9,
   "<15em,-6em>*+{\\map {G \\tuple{-, D} } {C'} } = \"GC2D\","
  ],
  [
   10,
   ""
  ],
  [
   11,
   "\"FCD\";\"FC2D\" **@{-} ?>*@{>} ?<>(.5)*!/_1em/{\\map {F \\tuple{-, D} } f },"
  ],
  [
   12,
   "\"GCD\";\"GC2D\" **@{-} ?>*@{>} ?<>(.5)*!/^1em/{\\map {F \\tuple{-, D} } f },"
  ],
  [
   13,
   "\"FCD\";\"GCD\" **@{-} ?>*@{>} ?<>(.5)*!/^3em/{\\alpha \\tuple{-, D}_C },"
  ],
  [
   14,
   "\"FC2D\";\"GC2D\" **@{-} ?>*@{>} ?<>(.5)*!/_3em/{\\alpha \\tuple{-, D}_{C'} },"
  ],
  [
   15,
   ""
  ],
  [
   16,
   "<0em,-12em>*+{\\map {F \\tuple{C', -} } D} = \"FC2D\","
  ],
  [
   17,
   "<15em,-12em>*+{\\map {F \\tuple{C', -} } {D'} } = \"FC2D2\","
  ],
  [
   18,
   "<0em,-18em>*+{\\map {G \\tuple{C', -} } D} = \"GC2D\","
  ],
  [
   19,
   "<15em,-18em>*+{\\map {G \\tuple{C', -} } {D'} } = \"GC2D2\","
  ],
  [
   20,
   ""
  ],
  [
   21,
   "\"FC2D\";\"FC2D2\" **@{-} ?>*@{>} ?<>(.5)*!/_1em/{\\map {F \\tuple{C', -} } g},"
  ],
  [
   22,
   "\"GC2D\";\"GC2D2\" **@{-} ?>*@{>} ?<>(.5)*!/^1em/{\\map {G \\tuple{C', -} } g},"
  ],
  [
   23,
   "\"FC2D\";\"GC2D\" **@{-} ?>*@{>} ?<>(.5)*!/^3em/{\\alpha \\tuple{C', -}_D },"
  ],
  [
   24,
   "\"FC2D2\";\"GC2D2\" **@{-} ?>*@{>} ?<>(.5)*!/_3em/{\\alpha \\tuple{C', -}_{D'} },"
  ],
  [
   25,
   "\\end{xy}$</nowiki>"
  ],
  [
   26,
   ""
  ],
  [
   27,
   "That is:"
  ],
  [
   28,
   ":for all [[Definition:Morphism (Category Theory)|morphisms]] $\\tuple{f: C \\to C', g: D \\to D'} \\in \\mathbf C \\times \\mathbf D$ the following [[Definition:Commutative Diagram|diagram commutes]]:"
  ],
  [
   29,
   ""
  ],
  [
   30,
   "::<nowiki>$\\begin{xy}"
  ],
  [
   31,
   "<0em,0em>*+{\\map F {C, D} } = \"FCD\","
  ],
  [
   32,
   "<12em,0em>*+{\\map F {C', D} } = \"FC2D\","
  ],
  [
   33,
   "<24em,0em>*+{\\map F {C', D'} } = \"FC2D2\","
  ],
  [
   34,
   "<0em,-6em>*+{\\map G {C, D} } = \"GCD\","
  ],
  [
   35,
   "<12em,-6em>*+{\\map G {C', D} } = \"GC2D\","
  ],
  [
   36,
   "<24em,-6em>*+{\\map G {C', D'} } = \"GC2D2\","
  ],
  [
   37,
   ""
  ],
  [
   38,
   "\"FCD\";\"FC2D\" **@{-} ?>*@{>} ?<>(.5)*!/_1em/{\\map F {f, \\operatorname{id}_D} },"
  ],
  [
   39,
   "\"GCD\";\"GC2D\" **@{-} ?>*@{>} ?<>(.5)*!/^1em/{\\map G {f, \\operatorname{id}_D} },"
  ],
  [
   40,
   "\"FCD\";\"GCD\" **@{-} ?>*@{>} ?<>(.5)*!/^2em/{\\alpha_{\\tuple{C, D} } },"
  ],
  [
   41,
   "\"FC2D\";\"GC2D\" **@{-} ?>*@{>} ?<>(.5)*!/_2em/{\\alpha_{\\tuple{C', D} } },"
  ],
  [
   42,
   "\"FC2D\";\"FC2D2\" **@{-} ?>*@{>} ?<>(.5)*!/_1em/{\\map F {\\operatorname{id}_{C'}, g} },"
  ],
  [
   43,
   "\"GC2D\";\"GC2D2\" **@{-} ?>*@{>} ?<>(.5)*!/^1em/{\\map G {\\operatorname{id}_{C'}, g} },"
  ],
  [
   44,
   "\"FC2D2\";\"GC2D2\" **@{-} ?>*@{>} ?<>(.5)*!/_2em/{\\alpha_{\\tuple{C', D'} } },"
  ],
  [
   45,
   "\\end{xy}$</nowiki>"
  ],
  [
   46,
   "by definitions of "
  ],
  [
   47,
   ":* [[Definition:Functor|functors]] obtained by [[Definition:Bifunctor|substituting the first variable]] and [[Definition:Bifunctor|substituting the second variable]]"
  ],
  [
   48,
   ":* $\\alpha \\tuple{C, -}$ and $\\alpha \\tuple{-, D}$"
  ],
  [
   49,
   ""
  ],
  [
   50,
   "By definition of [[Definition:Bifunctor|bifunctor]] and [[Definition:Identity Morphism|identity morphism]]:"
  ],
  [
   51,
   ":for all [[Definition:Morphism (Category Theory)|morphisms]] $\\tuple{f: C \\to C', g: D \\to D'} \\in \\mathbf C \\times \\mathbf D$ the following [[Definition:Commutative Diagram|diagram commutes]]:"
  ],
  [
   52,
   ""
  ],
  [
   53,
   "::<nowiki>$\\begin{xy}"
  ],
  [
   54,
   "<0em,4em>*+{\\map F {C, D} } = \"FCD\","
  ],
  [
   55,
   "<12em,0em>*+{\\map F {C', D} } = \"FC2D\","
  ],
  [
   56,
   "<24em,4em>*+{\\map F {C', D'} } = \"FC2D2\","
  ],
  [
   57,
   "<0em,-10em>*+{\\map G {C, D} } = \"GCD\","
  ],
  [
   58,
   "<12em,-6em>*+{\\map G {C', D} } = \"GC2D\","
  ],
  [
   59,
   "<24em,-10em>*+{\\map G {C', D'} } = \"GC2D2\","
  ],
  [
   60,
   ""
  ],
  [
   61,
   "\"FCD\";\"FC2D\" **@{-} ?>*@{>} ?<>(.5)*!/^1.5em/{\\map F {f, \\operatorname{id}_D} },"
  ],
  [
   62,
   "\"GCD\";\"GC2D\" **@{-} ?>*@{>} ?<>(.5)*!/_1.5em/{\\map G {f, \\operatorname{id}_D} },"
  ],
  [
   63,
   "\"FCD\";\"GCD\" **@{-} ?>*@{>} ?<>(.5)*!/^2em/{\\alpha_{\\tuple{C, D} } },"
  ],
  [
   64,
   "\"FC2D\";\"GC2D\" **@{-} ?>*@{>} ?<>(.5)*!/_2em/{\\alpha_{\\tuple{C', D} } },"
  ],
  [
   65,
   "\"FC2D\";\"FC2D2\" **@{-} ?>*@{>} ?<>(.5)*!/^1.5em/{\\map F {\\operatorname{id}_{C'}, g} },"
  ],
  [
   66,
   "\"GC2D\";\"GC2D2\" **@{-} ?>*@{>} ?<>(.5)*!/_1.5em/{\\map G {\\operatorname{id}_{C'}, g} },"
  ],
  [
   67,
   "\"FC2D2\";\"GC2D2\" **@{-} ?>*@{>} ?<>(.5)*!/_2em/{\\alpha_{\\tuple{C', D'} } },"
  ],
  [
   68,
   "\"FCD\";\"FC2D2\" **@{-} ?>*@{>} ?<>(.5)*!/_1em/{\\map F {f,g} },"
  ],
  [
   69,
   "\"GCD\";\"GC2D2\" **@{-} ?>*@{>} ?<>(.5)*!/^1em/{\\map G {f,g} },"
  ],
  [
   70,
   "\\end{xy}$</nowiki>"
  ],
  [
   71,
   ""
  ],
  [
   72,
   "It follows that $\\alpha : F \\to G$ is a [[Definition:Natural Transformation|natural transformation]] by definition.{{qed}}"
  ],
  [
   73,
   ""
  ],
  [
   74,
   "== Proof 2 =="
  ],
  [
   75,
   "By definition of [[Definition:Natural Transformation|natural transformation]]:"
  ],
  [
   76,
   ":for all [[Definition:Morphism (Category Theory)|morphisms]] $f: C \\to C' \\in \\mathbf C$ and $g:D \\to D' \\in \\mathbf D$:"
  ],
  [
   77,
   "::$\\map {G \\tuple{-, D} } f \\circ \\alpha \\tuple{-, D}_C = \\alpha \\tuple{-, D}_{C'} \\circ \\map {F \\tuple{-, D} } f$"
  ],
  [
   78,
   "::$\\map {G \\tuple{C, -} } g \\circ \\alpha \\tuple{C, -}_D = \\alpha \\tuple{C, -}_{D'} \\circ \\map {F \\tuple{C, -} } g$"
  ],
  [
   79,
   ""
  ],
  [
   80,
   "That is "
  ],
  [
   81,
   ":for all [[Definition:Morphism (Category Theory)|morphisms]] $f: C \\to C' \\in \\mathbf C$ and $g:D \\to D' \\in \\mathbf D$:"
  ],
  [
   82,
   "::$(3)\\quad \\map G {f, \\operatorname{id}_D} \\circ \\alpha_{\\tuple{C, D} } = \\alpha_{\\tuple{C', D} } \\circ \\map G {f, \\operatorname{id}_D}$"
  ],
  [
   83,
   "::$(4)\\quad \\map G {\\operatorname{id}_C, g} \\circ \\alpha_{\\tuple{C, D} } = \\alpha_{\\tuple{C, D'} } \\circ \\map F {\\operatorname{id}_C, g}$"
  ],
  [
   84,
   "by definitions of "
  ],
  [
   85,
   ":* [[Definition:Functor|functors]] obtained by [[Definition:Bifunctor|substituting the first variable]] and [[Definition:Bifunctor|substituting the second variable]]"
  ],
  [
   86,
   ":* $\\alpha \\tuple{C, -}$ and $\\alpha \\tuple{-, D}$"
  ],
  [
   87,
   ""
  ],
  [
   88,
   "For all [[Definition:Morphism (Category Theory)|morphisms]] $\\tuple{f: C \\to C', g:D \\to D'} \\in \\mathbf C \\times \\mathbf D$, we have:"
  ],
  [
   89,
   "{{begin-eqn}}"
  ],
  [
   90,
   "{{eqn | l = \\map G {f, g} \\circ \\alpha_{\\tuple{C, D} }"
  ],
  [
   91,
   "      | r = \\map G {\\operatorname{id}_{C'} \\circ f, g \\circ \\operatorname{id}_D} \\circ \\alpha_{\\tuple{C, D} }"
  ],
  [
   92,
   "      | c = {{Defof|Identity Morphism}}"
  ],
  [
   93,
   "}}"
  ],
  [
   94,
   "{{eqn | r = \\map G {\\tuple{\\operatorname{id}_{C'}, g} \\circ \\tuple{f, \\operatorname{id}_D} } \\circ \\alpha_{\\tuple{C, D} }"
  ],
  [
   95,
   "      | c = {{Defof|Product Category|Composition in Product Category}}"
  ],
  [
   96,
   "}}"
  ],
  [
   97,
   "{{eqn | r = \\map G {\\operatorname{id}_{C'}, g} \\circ \\map G {f, \\operatorname{id}_D} \\circ \\alpha_{\\tuple{C, D} }"
  ],
  [
   98,
   "      | c = {{Defof|Bifunctor}}"
  ],
  [
   99,
   "}}"
  ],
  [
   100,
   "{{eqn | r = \\map G {\\operatorname{id}_{C'}, g} \\circ \\alpha_{\\tuple{C', D} } \\circ \\map F {f, \\operatorname{id}_D}"
  ],
  [
   101,
   "      | c = By $(3)$"
  ],
  [
   102,
   "}}"
  ],
  [
   103,
   "{{eqn | r = \\alpha_{\\tuple{C', D'} } \\circ \\map F {\\operatorname{id}_{C'}, g} \\circ \\map F {f, \\operatorname{id}_D}"
  ],
  [
   104,
   "      | c = By $(4)$"
  ],
  [
   105,
   "}}"
  ],
  [
   106,
   "{{eqn | r = \\alpha_{\\tuple{C', D'} } \\circ \\map F {\\tuple{\\operatorname{id}_{C'}, g} \\circ \\tuple{f, \\operatorname{id}_{D} } }"
  ],
  [
   107,
   "      | c = {{Defof|Bifunctor}}"
  ],
  [
   108,
   "}}"
  ],
  [
   109,
   "{{eqn | r = \\alpha_{\\tuple{C', D'} } \\circ \\map F {\\operatorname{id}_{C'} \\circ f, g \\circ  \\operatorname{id}_{D} }"
  ],
  [
   110,
   "      | c = {{Defof|Product Category|Composition in Product Category}}"
  ],
  [
   111,
   "}}"
  ],
  [
   112,
   "{{eqn | r = \\alpha_{\\tuple{C', D'} } \\circ \\map F {f, g}"
  ],
  [
   113,
   "      | c = {{Defof|Identity Morphism}}"
  ],
  [
   114,
   "}}"
  ],
  [
   115,
   "{{end-eqn}}"
  ],
  [
   116,
   ""
  ],
  [
   117,
   "It follows that $\\alpha: F \\to G$ is a [[Definition:Natural Transformation|natural transformation]] by definition.{{qed}}"
